@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
top to bottom direction
title TurboWin+ responsibilities (one desktop application)

actor "Ship observer" as Observer
component "Instruments / GPS\nVaisala, Mintaka, EUCAWS, OMC-140" as Sensors
component "Email server /\ndesktop mail client" as Email
component "Observation server\nHTTP / HTTPS" as HTTP
component "Java Format 101\nencoder" as Format101

component "TurboWin+" as TurboWin {
  component "Swing forms /\nlegacy entry points" as UI
  component "Startup / configuration\nworkflows" as Startup
  component "Device workflows /\nrecord parsers" as Acquisition
  component "Shared mutable state\nmain, main_RS232_RS422, my*" as State
  component "Output preparation /\ndispatch workflows" as Output
  component "Validation /\ndomain calculations" as Validation
  component "Observation coding /\nFormat 101 preparation" as Coding
  component "Transport workflows /\nresult handlers" as Transport
  component "Statistics / graphs / maps" as Views
  folder "Local text files\nconfiguration, IMMT, system logs, sensor history" as Files
}

Observer --> UI : enter observations
Sensors --> Acquisition : records
UI --> Startup : initialize
Startup --> State : configuration / initialization
UI --> State : input / display fields
Acquisition --> State : measurements
Acquisition --> Files : sensor history
UI --> Output : choose output
Output ..> State : reads / updates
Output --> Validation : path-specific checks
Output --> Coding : compose
Output --> Transport : dispatch
Output --> Files : logs / exports
Startup --> Files : configuration
UI --> Views
Views --> Files : read logs / history
Transport --> Email
Transport --> HTTP
Coding --> Format101

note bottom of State
  Logical responsibilities, not isolated services.
  Many workflows also access globals directly;
  not all shared-state dependencies are drawn.
end note

note bottom of Files
  File-based persistence, not a database.
  Logging/reset is not proof of delivery.
end note

@enduml
